Save93 / Whiterun exterior / native FIFO and lock context at tasklet completion / 2026-11-09

Setup and method
- Skyrim AE 1.6.1170.0, original Save93 copied to the existing disposable profile, SSE Display Tweaks 0.5.16 with its 42 FPS gameplay cap and dynamic Papyrus budget. Frame generation was disabled only in the disposable profile. One save load, four Bannered Mare to WhiterunWorld transitions, 32 Utility.Wait(0.01) probes per trial.
- Only tag depth-one stock ObjectReference.GetWorldSpace calls from DynDOLOD ObjectEnabler OnCellAttach or OnCellDetach while the stack owns the root Papyrus lock. The verified stock function and query are passed unchanged to the original enqueue. A thread-local tag links publication and original VMProcess return for the same stack. The queue observation compares the original query identity under the stock funcQueueLock and reads current root-lock ownership without modifying it.
- Compare render frame, actual FIFO head and its next stock pop, caller RVA, stock VM::Update boundary, owner of frozenStacksLock, and whether the return executes inside the stock native phase. Separately observe the direct local VM::UpdateTasklets boundary, if taken.
- Live executable 104767 acquires frozenStacksLock at RVA 0x144428B before calling the native drain at 0x144430F. Observed tasklet return RVA 0xCF7888 follows the indirect callback at 0xCF7885 in the job dispatcher. The dispatcher accounts for job completion with its decrement at 0xCF78A7, after the individual tasklet observer returns. The direct VM::UpdateTasklets call site returns at 0x14449BF and was not observed in the measured windows.
- Initial launch stopped before Save93 loaded because the tracer exhausted its trampoline allocation. The completed build reserves 512 bytes for this diagnostic mode only. Exact runtime byte and vtable checks, xmake test build, budget policy checks, and synthetic finish/FIFO/frame/thread/lock validation passed.
- Completed capture build/gameplay-trace/cell-42-getworldspace-finish-observe-retry. DLL SHA256 E734A2720C6C38EE740D5866D20B3B5184E55101DD9439F95CB7066DA9BBDA64.

