Interpretation
- Of 84 holder GetWorldSpace calls, 79 were published after a previous drain's last decision. All 79 were traced through same-render-frame VMProcess completion and BSJobs callback return, after the preceding VM::Update exited. Sixty ran on a different thread from the drain; nineteen ran on the same thread.
- For 78 of the 79, another native message was first at tasklet return. The observed head remained the first stack popped at the following stock drain in every case. The one exact head also retained its original root lock and ran on the preceding drain thread (trial 2, stack 1487727), but owned neither the stock VM freeze guard nor the stock native execution phase. It waited 15.1997 ms from tasklet return to the next drain. None of the 160 tagged tasklet completions owned the freeze guard or were in the original native phase. All 1520 observed stock drain starts owned that guard.
- The individual tasklet completion point produced zero candidates satisfying both FIFO and existing native context. The direct local tasklet batch route was not used. The observation does not establish a later synchronized BSJobs batch-completion site. No accelerated path was installed, and the four stock metrics are a baseline only.

